# Godot 4 — rebuilt on import, never commit
.godot/
.import/

# Godot imports `audit/suite_audit.csv` with the `csv_translation` importer — it sees a .csv
# and assumes a translation table — so it emits one binary `.translation` per COLUMN beside the
# source. Nothing loads them: `run_suite.gd` writes the CSV and `test_suite_audit_csv.gd` reads
# it, both through plain FileAccess. They were tracked, so every regenerated audit put nine
# binaries in the diff. A tenth, `suite_audit.description.translation`, was tracked from a
# retired column set: deleting all ten and re-importing brought back exactly the nine the
# .import lists, which is how the orphan was identified rather than assumed.
# Deleting them is not the fix — the importer would just remake them; changing the CSV's
# import type to "keep" would, and that is a project.godot/.import decision, not an ignore one.
audit/*.translation

# Checkpoint artifacts (taskblock-41 Pass E) are LOCAL ONLY. Real sizes: ~72K
# and ~180K for the two stills checkpoints, 484K for the one carrying a video,
# 43-58K per 1920x1080 PNG. Thousands are affordable on local disk and none of
# them belong in git. The durable record of a checkpoint is the ANSWERS to its
# checklist, which go in reports/Report-TaskblockN.md.
out/checkpoints/

# Export artifacts
export_presets.cfg
*.tmp

# Cloned GUT working dir if you clone to repo root by mistake
/tmp/gut/

# Local build/workflow notes — not published
/CLAUDE.md

# Taskblock specs are working notes, not records. reports/ is the record.
# A spec with passes that were never executed reads as work that did not happen.
/taskblock*.md
/taskblock_done/

# Per-pass completion times, a scratch record for the session that is running the block.
# LOCAL ONLY and deliberately ignored: pass commits use `git add -A`, so an untracked file in
# the root would otherwise ride along into whichever pass happened to land next.
/tb*-pass-times.md

# Regenerated every run.
/out/combat.log
# taskblock-52: rotated per-session logs (FileSink.ARCHIVE_DIR)
/out/logs/

# Failure-ordering history (taskblock-50 Pass E1) — a LOCAL learning cache.
# Written on every ordered run so it can learn; committing it would put churn in
# every diff and make one machine's flakes everyone else's run order.
out/suite_failures.json

# Supervisor scratch pad for the live bug hunts — deliberately untracked.
temp.md

# Editor swap/backup files. `.BUGS.md.kate-swp` was committed by a `git add -A` while the
# supervisor had the ledger open, so this is a rule earned rather than anticipated: the
# living docs are edited during the same sessions CC commits from, and a swap file caught
# mid-write is a snapshot of a half-typed entry.
.*.kate-swp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
